.TH P3M-MV 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-mv \- parallel move
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-mv
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR SOURCE ...
.I DEST
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-mv
moves files and directory trees in parallel.
On the same file system a subtree moves with a single
.BR rename (2),
which is instant regardless of size.
Across file systems it is copied in parallel with full metadata preservation
and each source entry is removed only after its copy has fully succeeded.
.PP
Unlike
.BR mv (1),
an existing destination directory is
.I merged
rather than refused; each conflict-free subtree still moves by rename.
Emptied source directories are removed deepest-first; a directory that still
holds skipped entries is kept, so a skipped conflict never loses data.
.PP
By default this is a
.B dry run
listing what would happen (with rename/copy prediction); add
.B \-\-apply
to move.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually move (the default is a dry run).
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace existing destination entries; without it they are skipped and their
sources kept.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown, and a
.B \-o
file is still written.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH SAFETY
The file system root can never be a source; this guard cannot be overridden.
.B .
and
.B ..
are refused, as are moves of a directory into itself.
Symbolic links are moved as links and never followed.
.SH SIGNALS
On the first
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
during
.BR \-\-apply ,
.B p3m-mv
prints a notice, stops picking up new work and lets every in-flight rename or
cross-device copy finish.
A source file is never deleted before its destination is completely written,
and no destination is left truncated; entries not yet reached stay where they
are.
The summary reports
.B interrupted
and the exit status is 130 (SIGINT) or 143 (SIGTERM).
A second signal terminates immediately; at worst one in-flight destination
file is left partial, with its source intact.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (skipped existing destinations are not errors).
.TP
.B 1
Completed with errors.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, root-guard or into-itself refusal.
.TP
.BR 130 ", " 143
Interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
p3m\-mv /data/incoming /data/archive
p3m\-mv \-\-apply /data/incoming /data/archive
p3m\-mv \-\-apply \-j 16 /scratch/run42 /mnt/nfs/results
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-cp (1),
.BR p3m\-rm (1),
.BR mv (1)
